comments.content:
N+1 query inside the record loop. For every row this issues `customerMapper.selectById`, `deptMapper.selectById` and `userMapper.selectById`, and then calls `hasPoolPerm` three times — which itself runs `configMapper.selectById(poolId)` for every non-admin call (see SeaConfigService#hasPoolPerm line 140). A 20-row page therefore generates up to 20*(3+3)=~120 extra queries. Suggest batch-fetching the related entities and hoisting the per-user / per-pool work out of the loop, e.g.:

```java
List<BizSeaPool> records = page.getRecords();
Set<Long> customerIds = records.stream().map(BizSeaPool::getCustomerId).filter(Objects::nonNull).collect(toSet());
Map<Long, BizCustomer> customerMap = customerIds.isEmpty() ? Map.of()
        : customerMapper.selectBatchIds(customerIds).stream().collect(toMap(BizCustomer::getId, identity()));
Set<Long> officeIds = customerMap.values().stream().map(BizCustomer::getOfficeId).filter(Objects::nonNull).collect(toSet());
Map<Long, SysDept> deptMap = officeIds.isEmpty() ? Map.of()
        : deptMapper.selectBatchIds(officeIds).stream().collect(toMap(SysDept::getId, identity()));
Set<Long> ownerIds = records.stream().map(BizSeaPool::getOriginalOwnerId).filter(Objects::nonNull).collect(toSet());
Map<Long, SysUser> userMap = ownerIds.isEmpty() ? Map.of()
        : userMapper.selectBatchIds(ownerIds).stream().collect(toMap(SysUser::getId, identity()));

SecurityUser currentUser = SecurityUtils.getCurrentUser();
Map<Long, Boolean> editCache = new HashMap<>(), deleteCache = new HashMap<>(), claimCache = new HashMap<>();
```

