Every endpoint hardcodes the `/sea` resource prefix repeatedly (11 occurrences). This duplicates the base path across the module: when the API prefix changes (e.g. `/sea` → `/api/sea` or a versioned prefix) every function must be edited, and typos are easy to introduce. Extract the prefix into a single module-level constant and build the paths from it, e.g.:

```js
const SEA_BASE = '/sea'
export function getSeaList(params) {
  return request.get(`${SEA_BASE}/list`, { params })
}
```

